      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for pointing this out. I wasn\u0027t aware that with a zero timeout,\nrequestStop() cannot wake monitor() while the line is idle. In our\ncurrent use case, GPIOValve always passes 1 second, so this situation\ndoesn\u0027t happen.\n\nNow monitor() rejects a zero timeout by throwing std::invalid_argument,\nwhich makes sure every caller of monitor() passes a valid timeout.\nstart() still accepts zero for existing users such as leakdetector.",
